  user_input {
    user_response: "Role: You are a Senior AI Vision Engineer specializing in Google technologies (MediaPipe, TensorFlow.js, and Gemini Multimodal).\nObjective: Build a web-based prototype for an \"Airline Agent Presence Trainer.\" The app must provide real-time feedback to trainees on their professionalism by analyzing video via the webcam.\nCore Requirements & Logic:\nPosture Analysis (using MediaPipe Pose):\nTrack landmarks for Ears, Shoulders, Hips, and Knees.\nLogic: Calculate the vertical alignment. If the \"Ear-Shoulder-Hip\" angle is less than 165 degrees, flag \"Slouching.\"\nLogic: Check if shoulders are level. If the Y-coordinate difference between left and right shoulders is > 5%, flag \"Uneven Stance.\"\nFacial Expression & Engagement (using MediaPipe Face Mesh):\nLogic: Detect \"Smile Rate\" by measuring the distance between the corners of the mouth.\nLogic: Detect \"Eye Contact\" by calculating the gaze vector (Iris tracking) relative to the camera.\nLogic: Detect \"Approachability\" (relaxed brow vs. furrowed brow).\nPhysical Attributes & Grooming (using Gemini 1.5 Pro Multimodal):\nEvery 10 seconds, capture a frame and send it to Gemini to check:\nIs the airline scarf/tie straight?\nIs the name badge visible and upright?\nIs the agent\'s hair within professional \"aviation standards\" (neat/tied back)?\nTech Stack:\nFrontend: HTML5, CSS (Modern/Clean \"Aviation\" UI), and TypeScript/JavaScript.\nAI Engine: Google MediaPipe (for real-time skeleton/face landmarks).\nBackend/Logic: TensorFlow.js for on-device processing.\nFeedback UI: A \"Professionalism Meter\" (0-100%) and a \"Live Suggestions\" ticker (e.g., \"Smile more,\" \"Straighten your back\").\nDeliverables:\nProvide a complete single-file HTML/JavaScript solution that I can run in a browser.\nInclude the mathematical functions for calculating posture angles.\nUse a \"Virtual Mirror\" overlay style where the skeleton and face mesh are drawn over the user\'s video in real-time.\nSet the styling to be \"Airlines Brand\" inspired (Navy Blue, Gold, White, clean typography).\n"
    items {
      text: "Role: You are a Senior AI Vision Engineer specializing in Google technologies (MediaPipe, TensorFlow.js, and Gemini Multimodal).\nObjective: Build a web-based prototype for an \"Airline Agent Presence Trainer.\" The app must provide real-time feedback to trainees on their professionalism by analyzing video via the webcam.\nCore Requirements & Logic:\nPosture Analysis (using MediaPipe Pose):\nTrack landmarks for Ears, Shoulders, Hips, and Knees.\nLogic: Calculate the vertical alignment. If the \"Ear-Shoulder-Hip\" angle is less than 165 degrees, flag \"Slouching.\"\nLogic: Check if shoulders are level. If the Y-coordinate difference between left and right shoulders is > 5%, flag \"Uneven Stance.\"\nFacial Expression & Engagement (using MediaPipe Face Mesh):\nLogic: Detect \"Smile Rate\" by measuring the distance between the corners of the mouth.\nLogic: Detect \"Eye Contact\" by calculating the gaze vector (Iris tracking) relative to the camera.\nLogic: Detect \"Approachability\" (relaxed brow vs. furrowed brow).\nPhysical Attributes & Grooming (using Gemini 1.5 Pro Multimodal):\nEvery 10 seconds, capture a frame and send it to Gemini to check:\nIs the airline scarf/tie straight?\nIs the name badge visible and upright?\nIs the agent\'s hair within professional \"aviation standards\" (neat/tied back)?\nTech Stack:\nFrontend: HTML5, CSS (Modern/Clean \"Aviation\" UI), and TypeScript/JavaScript.\nAI Engine: Google MediaPipe (for real-time skeleton/face landmarks).\nBackend/Logic: TensorFlow.js for on-device processing.\nFeedback UI: A \"Professionalism Meter\" (0-100%) and a \"Live Suggestions\" ticker (e.g., \"Smile more,\" \"Straighten your back\").\nDeliverables:\nProvide a complete single-file HTML/JavaScript solution that I can run in a browser.\nInclude the mathematical functions for calculating posture angles.\nUse a \"Virtual Mirror\" overlay style where the skeleton and face mesh are drawn over the user\'s video in real-time.\nSet the styling to be \"Airlines Brand\" inspired (Navy Blue, Gold, White, clean typography).\n"
    }
  }
}
