  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Objective**\n\nI\'m digging into the specifics of this user request. The core is an \"Airline Agent Presence Trainer\" web app. I\'ve pinpointed the key requirements, like real-time webcam feedback for trainees on professionalism. This gives me a solid starting point for further design considerations.\n\n\n**Defining the AI Workflow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the AI component. Posture will be assessed with MediaPipe Pose, looking at landmark angles for slouching and shoulder differences. Face Mesh (or Landmarker) will provide the smile, gaze, and brow analysis. I\'ll integrate Gemini 1.5 Pro to periodically analyze image frames for tie/scarf straightness, name badge visibility, and hair compliance, all on 10 second intervals. The user interface will be simple and professional.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Tech Stack**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The instructions\' conflicting directives on client-side versus full-stack architecture are causing a rethink. The original plan leaned client-side but the Gemini API necessitates a server-side route for API key protection. I\'m now certain this requires a full-stack solution with Express and Vite.\n\n\n**Assessing the Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on available skills. I\'ve performed a skill check, and identified the \"gemini-api\" and \"image-generation\" as relevant. The Gemini API is crucial for the grooming analysis, while image generation could provide visual enhancements if needed. Other skills are deemed irrelevant, which means a leaner design!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 741584810
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
