    thinking: "**Considering Model Selection**\n\nI\'ve determined that the Gemini API is easy to work with. I think `gemini-3.5-flash` is a strong candidate for generating the content payload, specifically for multimodal tasks like the scarf, name tag, and alignment checks, but I\'ll also consider other viable models like `gemini-3.5-flash` because it excels in this area.\n\n\n**Analyzing Posture & Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on posture and facial analysis. My current approach involves MediaPipe Pose for landmark tracking, specifically ears, shoulders, hips, and knees. I\'m calculating the Ear-Shoulder-Hip angle, flagging slouching if it\'s below 165 degrees, and checking for uneven stance based on shoulder Y-coordinate differences exceeding 5%. I\'ve also started working on facial expression recognition using MediaPipe Face Mesh, exploring the smile rate, eye contact, and approachability.\n\n\n"
