  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing the App**\n\nI\'ve got the modular UI components prepped. Now I\'m diving into `/src/App.tsx`, focusing on its coordination role. I\'m currently defining state variables. I\'ve begun with `poseMetrics` and `facialMetrics`, but need to continue.\n\n\n**Defining State Variables**\n\nI\'m now expanding the state variables within `/src/App.tsx`. I\'ve added `groomingMetrics`, `sessionLogs` (with local storage persistence), `nextCaptureInSeconds`, `autoCaptureActive`, `groomingLoading`, `mediaPipeRunning`, and `cameraError`. I am also implementing React Refs: `videoRef`, `canvasRef`, `poseRef`, `faceRef`, `cameraRef`, `latestPoseRef`, and `latestFaceRef`. I\'m starting work on the web camera handling, including video frame processing via MediaPipe and a loading fallback.\n\n\n**Verifying MediaPipe Loading**\n\nI\'ve implemented a reliable check for MediaPipe scripts. I am now certain of their loading status, using a `setInterval` that clears when all required scripts are loaded. This involves checking for `window.Pose`, `window.FaceMesh`, and `window.Camera` every 500ms and setting `mediaPipeLoaded` accordingly. I also included a cleanup function.\n\n\n**Implementing Grooming Analysis**\n\nI\'m now integrating the grooming analysis. I\'m taking video frames, drawing them to an offscreen canvas for a clean capture, and converting them to a data URL. I am using the data URL to call the Express endpoint at `/api/analyze-grooming`, sending the image data in JSON format for analysis. I am handling potential errors in the API response. I am expecting the API to return a `GroomingMetrics` object, and handling the response accordingly.\n\n\n**Recording Session Logs**\n\nI\'ve incorporated automatic session logging now. Each capture records a `SessionHistoryLog` entry.  I am calculating an overall score. It is the average of posture, facial, and grooming standards. Posture depends on slouching and uneven stance. The facial score averages smile, eye contact, and approachability. I\'m storing each log with a unique ID and a timestamp, reflecting that I now have data for each session.\n\n\n**Finalizing Score Calculation**\n\nI\'ve finalized the score calculation and session logging. I\'m now integrating all metrics from posture, facial, and grooming into unified historical training runs. I\'m automatically recording each session with persistent storage via local storage. Each log includes timestamps and unique IDs. The comprehensive structure now provides a complete training record!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 126629274
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
