  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Errors**\n\nI\'m currently focused on addressing the app errors. Error logs point to a failure in the `/api/analyze-grooming` backend call. Specifically, I\'m seeing a 503 error, indicating the model is overloaded, preventing analysis. My priority is to pinpoint why the model is experiencing high load to fix the application\'s performance.\n\n\n**Addressing the Rate Limit**\n\nI\'ve made progress on the rate limiting issue. It seems the default `autoCaptureActive` setting, combined with its 10-second interval, is the culprit. I\'ve realized this aggressive behavior exhausts the free tier quota extremely fast, sometimes in a matter of minutes. To resolve this, I\'m now focusing on disabling `autoCaptureActive` by default. This change will prevent the application from making requests automatically and burning through the available requests too rapidly.\n\n\n**Implementing Fallback Strategies**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing a robust fallback strategy. The most recent focus is ensuring the application gracefully handles rate limits and API failures. My key update is the addition of a simulated assessment mode, using randomized but realistic variations of the captured input, and clearly labelling it as \'Offline/Simulation Warmup Mode\'. I\'m aiming for a seamless user experience, even when the API is unavailable, which is crucial for overall user satisfaction.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 213673591
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
